# keel's terminal app for the README's GIF (docs/gif/record-tui.sh): typed into the real app on a throw-away keel with
# keel's test model, on a full screen. Each @snap is one frame of the GIF; docs/gif/render-tui.py holds each frame.
@sleep 1500
@snap 01-start
@key shift+tab
@snap 02-mode-edit
@key shift+tab
@snap 03-mode-side
@key shift+tab
@snap 04-mode-ask
@type /flow feature Add a /health
@snap 05-type
@type  endpoint that answers {"ok": true}
@snap 06-typed
@key enter
@wait pick 60
@snap 07-pick
@key enter
@sleep 2500
@snap 08-running
@sleep 2500
@snap 09-running
@wait waiting 300
@key ctrl+f
@snap 10-gate-rail
@key ctrl+f
/status
@snap 11-status
@type What does the spec ask for?
@snap 12-ask
@key enter
@wait streaming 90
@snap 13-streaming
@sleep 900
@snap 14-streaming
@wait answer 240
@snap 15-answer
/diagram flow
@snap 16-diagram
